Subject: [DRAFT] win32u: Experiment with forwarding opaque cross-process GDI paints

Original code written with OpenAI Codex assistance; LGPL-2.1-or-later.
Not for submission to Wine and not enabled in normal builds.

Enable only in an experimental Wine runtime with WINE_WAYLAND_GDI_BRIDGE=1.
This is a diagnostic opaque-paint bridge, not a general rendering fix.
It must not be promoted without resolving transparent and destination-dependent
painting, dynamic clipping, resize/DPI/surface-generation races, synchronous
message waits, tile flush cost.
Initial independent review found no distinctive copied implementation; this
is not an exhaustive originality certification.

The standalone reproducer is documented in
 docs/wine-repro/winewayland-cross-process-gdi/README.md.
The full flake WoW64 build and opaque two-process screenshot test pass.
Inventor 2027.1 Home content is restored on isolated KWin at 150%, including
New/Cancel and normal exit with explicitly focused input. Focus artifacts and
other correctness/validation limits above remain; this is still a draft.

